    "collective_statement_most_likely_to_succeed": "The selected candidate successfully addresses all statutory and procedural requirements outlined in the Notice to File Missing Parts and the ATS brief. It affirmatively asserts Small Entity status under 37 CFR 1.27, which is critical for reducing the fee burden from undiscounted rates. The document executes a highly rewarded preemptive strike by filing a Substitute Specification under 37 CFR 1.125 to excise embedded drawings, segregate claims and the abstract to separate sheets (37 CFR 1.72(b), 1.75(h)), and remove inventor contact information from the specification body, thereby curing multiple formal defects simultaneously. Furthermore, it strictly adheres to the Path B Waterfall Strategy Directive by correctly identifying that no combination of unpaid fees fits within the $34.00 unapplied credit budget without exceeding it, thus allocating $0.00 from the credit and remitting the exact net fresh tender required ($970.00 for base fees plus a $60.00 suspension fee). The inclusion of a perfected declaration under 37 CFR 1.63 cures the final outstanding deficiency. The document is legally sound, procedurally precise, and optimally structured to advance the application out of pre-examination processing.",
